module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.CoherentCycle.MaximalDeltaDimension
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.ProperPushforwardPrincipal.DimensionDropApplications
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.AssociatedPoints.EmbeddedCharacterization

/-!
# Hypothesis (3) of Stacks 02S5, in the shape the source states it

Stacks 02S5 compares the two fibre cycles of a closed subscheme `Z ⊆ X ×_S 𝐏¹_S`. Its third
hypothesis is stated in the source for the *embedded* points of `Z` (Stacks 05AK): for any
embedded point `ξ` of `Z`, either `ξ ∉ Z₀ ∪ Z_∞` or `δ(ξ) < k`. The form
`Stacks.Chow.cycleAssociatedToFibres_rationallyEquivalent` imposes that condition at every
*associated* point of `Z`.

On a locally Noetherian scheme the associated points are the embedded ones together with the
generic points of the irreducible components
(`AlgebraicGeometry.isEmbeddedPoint_iff_not_genericPoint`, Stacks 05AL). This file states 02S5
with the source's clause verbatim and with the remaining content isolated as a second clause,
stated only where it has content: no irreducible component of `Z` of relative dimension exactly
`k` has its generic point on a distinguished section. At a generic point of relative dimension
below `k` the tag's disjunction holds outright, and at one of relative dimension above `k` the
delta-dimension bounds on the two fibres already keep it off both sections
(`Stacks.Chow.notMem_range_sections_of_lt_relativeDimension`), so those are the only generic
points the hypothesis has to mention.

## The second clause is not removable

The source's proof reads, at the generic point `ξ = (ξ', 0)` of a candidate integral closed
subscheme `Z' ⊆ X` of `δ`-dimension `k`: "By our choice of `ξ' ∈ Z'` we have `δ(ξ) = k` and
hence `dim(A/I) = 1`", for `A = 𝒪_{X ×_S 𝐏¹_S, ξ}` and `I` the ideal of `Z`. From `δ(ξ) = k`
and `dim_δ(Z) ≤ k + 1` one only gets `dim(A/I) ≤ 1`; equality fails exactly when `ξ` is a
generic point of an irreducible component of `Z`, in which case `I` is `𝔪`-primary. That case
is *not* excluded by hypothesis (3) as the source states it, because such a `ξ` is a maximal
associated point of `Z` and hence not an embedded point. The rest of the source's argument
breaks there: `dim(A/I) = 0` makes the local equation `t` of `X ×_S D₀` a zerodivisor on `A/I`,
the multiplicity `n = length_A(A/(t, I))` is at least `1` while the matching multiplicity
`m = ∑ length_A(A/(t, 𝔮ᵢ)) · length_{A_𝔮ᵢ}(A/I)_𝔮ᵢ` is an empty sum, and the claim
`[Z₀]_k = ∑ nᵢ[(Wᵢ)₀]_k` fails.

The conclusion of the lemma fails with it, so this is not a gap that better bookkeeping closes.
Take `S = Spec K` for a field `K` with `δ = 0` (`Stacks.Chow.fieldChowSituation`), `X = Spec K`,
`k = 0`, and for `Z` the image of the zero section `Spec K → 𝐏¹_K`. Then `dim_δ(Z) = 0 ≤ k + 1`,
`Z₀ = Z` has `dim_δ = 0 ≤ k`, `Z_∞ = ∅`, and `Z` is integral, so it has no embedded points at
all and the source's hypothesis (3) holds vacuously. But `[Z₀]₀ = [Spec K]` and `[Z_∞]₀ = 0`,
and a nonzero `0`-cycle on `Spec K` is not rationally equivalent to zero: by Stacks 02RW
rational equivalence of `0`-cycles is generated by principal divisors on integral closed
subschemes of `δ`-dimension `1`, of which `Spec K` has none, so the only `0`-cycle rationally
equivalent to zero on `Spec K` is `0` itself. The general shape of the obstruction is the same:
an irreducible component of `Z` of `δ`-dimension `k` contained in `Z₀` contributes to `[Z₀]_k`
and to no `[(Wᵢ)₀]_k`, and nothing cancels it in `[Z_∞]_k`.

Stacks uses 02S5 in exactly one place, the proof of Stacks 0FVJ (Lemma 42.67.4, change of base
scheme), and there the verification reads "Hence `W'` has no *associated* points lying on
`W'₀`" — the condition at associated points, not at embedded points. So the omission is in the
statement of the tag only; nothing downstream depends on the weaker reading.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.relativeDimension_familyBase_le_of_zeroSection` and its infinity twin — a point
  of `Z` on a distinguished section has relative dimension at most the delta-dimension of the
  corresponding fibre.
* `Stacks.Chow.notMem_range_sections_of_lt_relativeDimension` — hence a point of `Z` of relative
  dimension above `k` lies on neither section.
* `Stacks.Chow.sectionAvoidance_of_isEmbeddedPoint_of_genericPoints` — the condition at every
  associated point of `Z`, from the source's clause for embedded points together with the
  component clause.
* `Stacks.Chow.mem_schemeAssociatedPoints_of_isEmbeddedPoint` — an embedded point is an
  associated point, which with
  `AlgebraicGeometry.mem_schemeAssociatedPoints_of_isGenericPoint_irreducibleComponent` gives
  the converse implication, so neither form of the hypothesis is stronger than the other.
* `Stacks.Chow.cycleAssociatedToFibres_rationallyEquivalent_of_isEmbeddedPoint` — **Stacks
  02S5** with hypothesis (3) in the source's shape, plus the clause the source omits.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02S5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02S5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05AK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05AK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05AL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05AL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02RW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02RW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FVJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FVJ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType f] (k : ℤ)
  (Z : (projectiveLineProduct f).IdealSheafData)

/-! ### Points of `Z` on a distinguished section -/

/-- A point of a closed subscheme `W ⊆ X` of delta-dimension at most `k` has relative dimension
at most `k`. -/
private theorem relativeDimension_le_of_mem_support_of_schemeDeltaDimension_le
    (W : X.IdealSheafData) (hW : schemeDeltaDimension C (W.subschemeι ≫ f) ≤ (k : EInt)) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ (W.support : Set X)) : relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction f x ≤ k := by
  rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι] at hx
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hx
  exact relativeDimension_le_of_schemeDeltaDimension_le C f W.subschemeι hW y

/-- A point of `Z` lying on the zero section has relative dimension at most `k` as soon as the
zero fibre of `Z` has delta-dimension at most `k`. -/
theorem relativeDimension_familyBase_le_of_zeroSection
    (h₀ : schemeDeltaDimension C ((zeroFiber f Z).subschemeι ≫ f) ≤ (k : EInt))
    (ζ : Z.subscheme) (x : X) (hζ : Z.subschemeι ζ = zeroSection f x) :
    relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase f Z) ζ ≤ k := by
  rw [relativeDimension_familyBase_eq_of_zeroSection C f Z ζ x hζ]
  refine relativeDimension_le_of_mem_support_of_schemeDeltaDimension_le C f k _ h₀ ?_
  rw [coe_support_zeroFiber, ← Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
  exact ⟨ζ, hζ⟩

/-- A point of `Z` lying on the infinity section has relative dimension at most `k` as soon as
the infinity fibre of `Z` has delta-dimension at most `k`. -/
theorem relativeDimension_familyBase_le_of_infinitySection
    (hInf : schemeDeltaDimension C ((infinityFiber f Z).subschemeι ≫ f) ≤ (k : EInt))
    (ζ : Z.subscheme) (x : X) (hζ : Z.subschemeι ζ = infinitySection f x) :
    relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase f Z) ζ ≤ k := by
  rw [relativeDimension_familyBase_eq_of_infinitySection C f Z ζ x hζ]
  refine relativeDimension_le_of_mem_support_of_schemeDeltaDimension_le C f k _ hInf ?_
  rw [coe_support_infinityFiber, ← Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
  exact ⟨ζ, hζ⟩

/-- **Under the fibre bounds of Stacks 02S5, a point of `Z` of relative dimension above `k` lies
on neither distinguished section.** -/
theorem notMem_range_sections_of_lt_relativeDimension
    (h₀ : schemeDeltaDimension C ((zeroFiber f Z).subschemeι ≫ f) ≤ (k : EInt))
    (hInf : schemeDeltaDimension C ((infinityFiber f Z).subschemeι ≫ f) ≤ (k : EInt))
    (ζ : Z.subscheme) (hζ : k < relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase f Z) ζ) :
    Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (zeroSection f) ∧
      Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (infinitySection f) :=
  ⟨fun ⟨x, hx⟩ ↦
      absurd (relativeDimension_familyBase_le_of_zeroSection C f k Z h₀ ζ x hx.symm)
        (not_le.mpr hζ),
    fun ⟨x, hx⟩ ↦
      absurd (relativeDimension_familyBase_le_of_infinitySection C f k Z hInf ζ x hx.symm)
        (not_le.mpr hζ)⟩

/-! ### The two clauses of hypothesis (3) -/

/-- An embedded point of a locally Noetherian scheme is an associated point of it. -/
theorem mem_schemeAssociatedPoints_of_isEmbeddedPoint (Y : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    {y : Y} (hy : AlgebraicGeometry.IsEmbeddedPoint Y y) :
    y ∈ Stacks.Divisors.schemeAssociatedPoints Y :=
  ((AlgebraicGeometry.isEmbeddedPoint_iff_not_genericPoint Y y).mp hy).1

/-- **Hypothesis (3) of Stacks 02S5, at every associated point, from its two clauses.** The
associated points of a locally Noetherian scheme are its embedded points together with the
generic points of its irreducible components (Stacks 05AL); the condition holds at the former by
the source's clause `hEmbedded`, and at the latter by the component clause `hGeneric` together
with the fibre bounds `h₀` and `hInf`. -/
theorem sectionAvoidance_of_isEmbeddedPoint_of_genericPoints
    (h₀ : schemeDeltaDimension C ((zeroFiber f Z).subschemeι ≫ f) ≤ (k : EInt))
    (hInf : schemeDeltaDimension C ((infinityFiber f Z).subschemeι ≫ f) ≤ (k : EInt))
    (hEmbedded : ∀ ζ : Z.subscheme, AlgebraicGeometry.IsEmbeddedPoint Z.subscheme ζ →
      ((Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (zeroSection f) ∧
          Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (infinitySection f)) ∨
        relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase f Z) ζ < k))
    (hGeneric : ∀ ζ : Z.subscheme, ζ ∈ genericPoints Z.subscheme →
      relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase f Z) ζ = k →
      (Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (zeroSection f) ∧
        Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (infinitySection f)))
    (ζ : Z.subscheme) (hζ : ζ ∈ Stacks.Divisors.schemeAssociatedPoints Z.subscheme) :
    (Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (zeroSection f) ∧
        Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (infinitySection f)) ∨
      relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase f Z) ζ < k := by
  have _ : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  have _ : IsLocallyNoetherian Z.subscheme :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (familyBase f Z)
  by_cases hemb : AlgebraicGeometry.IsEmbeddedPoint Z.subscheme ζ
  · exact hEmbedded ζ hemb
  · have hgen : ζ ∈ genericPoints Z.subscheme := by
      rw [AlgebraicGeometry.isEmbeddedPoint_iff_not_genericPoint] at hemb
      push Not at hemb
      obtain ⟨T, hT, hTgen⟩ := hemb hζ
      change closure ({ζ} : Set Z.subscheme) ∈ irreducibleComponents Z.subscheme
      rwa [hTgen.def]
    rcases lt_trichotomy (relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase f Z) ζ) k with
      hlt | heq | hgt
    · exact Or.inr hlt
    · exact Or.inl (hGeneric ζ hgen heq)
    · exact Or.inl (notMem_range_sections_of_lt_relativeDimension C f k Z h₀ hInf ζ hgt)

/-! ### Stacks 02S5 -/

/-- **Stacks 02S5, with hypothesis (3) in the shape the source states it.** For a closed
subscheme `Z ⊆ X ×_S 𝐏¹_S` with `dim_δ(Z) ≤ k + 1` and `dim_δ(Z₀) ≤ k`, `dim_δ(Z_∞) ≤ k`, the
cycles of the two fibres are rationally equivalent on `X` as soon as

* `hEmbedded`, the source's hypothesis (3): every embedded point of `Z` either misses both
  distinguished sections or has relative dimension below `k`; and
* `hGeneric`, the clause the source omits: no irreducible component of `Z` of relative dimension
  exactly `k` has its generic point on a distinguished section.

`hGeneric` cannot be dropped — see the module documentation for an integral `Z` with no embedded
points at all for which the conclusion fails. Together the two clauses give the hypothesis of
`Stacks.Chow.cycleAssociatedToFibres_rationallyEquivalent`, by
`Stacks.Chow.sectionAvoidance_of_isEmbeddedPoint_of_genericPoints`, and are given by it, by
`Stacks.Chow.mem_schemeAssociatedPoints_of_isEmbeddedPoint` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_schemeAssociatedPoints_of_isGenericPoint_irreducibleComponent`. -/
@[stacks 02S5]
theorem cycleAssociatedToFibres_rationallyEquivalent_of_isEmbeddedPoint
    (hZ : ∀ ζ : Z.subscheme,
      relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase f Z) ζ ≤ k + 1)
    (h₀ : schemeDeltaDimension C ((zeroFiber f Z).subschemeι ≫ f) ≤ (k : EInt))
    (hInf : schemeDeltaDimension C ((infinityFiber f Z).subschemeι ≫ f) ≤ (k : EInt))
    (hEmbedded : ∀ ζ : Z.subscheme, AlgebraicGeometry.IsEmbeddedPoint Z.subscheme ζ →
      ((Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (zeroSection f) ∧
          Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (infinitySection f)) ∨
        relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase f Z) ζ < k))
    (hGeneric : ∀ ζ : Z.subscheme, ζ ∈ genericPoints Z.subscheme →
      relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase f Z) ζ = k →
      (Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (zeroSection f) ∧
        Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (infinitySection f))) :
    RationallyEquivalent C f k
      (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C f (zeroFiber f Z).subschemeι k)
      (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C f (infinityFiber f Z).subschemeι k) :=
  cycleAssociatedToFibres_rationallyEquivalent C f k Z hZ h₀ hInf
    (sectionAvoidance_of_isEmbeddedPoint_of_genericPoints C f k Z h₀ hInf hEmbedded hGeneric)

end Stacks.Chow

end
